Subject: [PATCH] kernelsu: run ksud again once /data is actually readable

On this device /data is not accessible when init reaches the post-fs-data
trigger, so the injected "exec ksud post-fs-data" cannot succeed and ksud
never runs at boot. init hits the same wall on its own commands:

  init: Top-level directory needs encryption action, eg mkdir /data/tombstones
  init: Command 'mkdir /data/tombstones 0771 system system' action=post-fs-data
        took 0ms and failed: lstat() failed on /data/tombstones: Permission denied

and the kernel's own throne_tracker gets -126 (ENOKEY) on
/data/system/packages.list at the same moment. Nothing module-related can
run that early: no module post-fs-data.sh, no service.sh, and no zygiskd,
which is why Zygisk modules report "Zygisk required" even with ReZygisk
installed. A soft reboot re-runs the whole sequence once /data is readable,
which is why it appears to fix everything.

This is the legacy fscrypt v1 + Qualcomm PFK/ICE arrangement this device
must keep, so the key cannot be made available earlier. Re-run ksud when
vold reports user 0's storage as available instead.

The existing post-fs-data trigger is deliberately kept rather than replaced:
on a boot where /data IS ready in time it still does the right thing, and on
this device it fails without side effects, so the later trigger is additive
rather than a duplicate run.

Note this cannot retroactively inject Zygisk into an already-running zygote;
it starts zygiskd, but zygote may still need restarting for Zygisk modules to
attach. That is the remaining known gap.

---
diff --git a/kernel/runtime/ksud_integration.c b/kernel/runtime/ksud_integration.c
--- a/kernel/runtime/ksud_integration.c
+++ b/kernel/runtime/ksud_integration.c
@@ -56,7 +56,15 @@ static const char KERNEL_SU_RC[] =
 	"on property:vold.decrypt=trigger_restart_framework\n"
 	"    exec u:r:" KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN ":s0 root -- " KSUD_PATH " services\n"
 	"\n"

+	// caymanslm: /data is unreadable at post-fs-data here, so the trigger
+	// above is too early for ksud to do anything. vold sets this once user
+	// 0's storage is usable.
+	"on property:sys.user.0.ce_available=true\n"
+	"    exec u:r:" KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN ":s0 root -- " KSUD_PATH " post-fs-data\n"
+	"    exec u:r:" KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN ":s0 root -- " KSUD_PATH " services\n"
+	"\n"
+
 	"on property:sys.boot_completed=1\n"
 	"    exec u:r:" KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN ":s0 root -- " KSUD_PATH " boot-completed\n"
 	"\n"
